WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Spy and the Salad</b>

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.700
<i>My name is Jean-François Mount de La Vigny.</i>

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.190
<b>Jean-François Mount de La Vigny (35)
 Collector of mysterious stories from Oilia. A spy.</b>

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:48.040
<i>I have infiltrated Aitheria on 
a secret mission from Oilia.</i>

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.760
<i>I'm a collector of mysterious stories. 
A story teller if you will.</i>

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>And a spy.</i>

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.460
<i>There was a horrible event that 
I, skilled story collector and</i>

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.470
<i>right-hand man of the director, 
witnessed myself directly.</i>

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.090
<i>I need to deliver this report to the 
motherland as soon as possible!</i>

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:11.290
<i>About that horrible event 
at that Izakaya Nobu!</i>

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:12.620
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:12.620
Welcome.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.360
<i>Quite passable for a tavern 
on the outskirts of town.</i>

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.690
<i>This is a perfect place for 
gathering information.</i>

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:30.300
<i>I, Jean-François Mount
de La Vigny, cannot be fooled!</i>

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.630
Here is an appetizer.

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.140
What is this exactly?

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.640
<b>Boiled Fava Beans With Salt</b>

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.640
<b>Despite looking firm, they have 
a soft texture. A gentle flavor</b>

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.660
These are fava beans boiled with 
salt. Please eat them as is.

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.350
What would you like to drink?

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:44.160
As you can see, I am a 
traveling man of the cloth.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.260
My profession does not allow me to drink.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.490
<b>Edwin (70)
 Deacon - Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.880
<i>I guess that is the local deacon.</i>

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:56.110
I would be happy if I could 
have some warm water.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:57.400
Right away.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:01.910
<i>Fava bean? I've never heard of such a bean. It must be a preserved food..</i>

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:06.270
I'm sure it can't compete
with our amuse-gueule.

00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:11.870
<i>Hm, this is not so bad.</i>

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.690
<i>Now, I suppose it is time to begin.</i>

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.150
Excuse me?

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:21.780
Yes?

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:23.790
May I have a salad, please?

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.250
<i>This is it! The information 
gathering technique that I,</i>

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.200
<i>the great Jean-François Mount
de La Vigny, have invented!</i>

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:33.260
<i>By assessing how many raw 
vegetables the country has</i>

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:35.430
<i>that can't be cooked into a 
main dish, I can ascertain</i>

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.840
<i>how well a country is doing!</i>

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.280
<i>In other words, the salad is 
a direct representation of</i>

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.300
<i>the power of that cit—
no, of the entire land!</i>

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.440
<i>This is what I, Jean-Fr—</i>

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.050
What kind of salad would you like?

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.940
My apologies. It is not too uncommon 
for a restaurant to not have salad.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.310
If you don't have any, I will... huh?

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.300
Wait, what kind?

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:00.350
Are you saying this place has 
multiple kinds of salads?!

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.050
Yes.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.170
<i>No way!</i>

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.060
<i>You can pick what kind of salad you 
want this far north in Aitheria?!</i>

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.070
<i>All right then!</i>

00:03:08.390 --> 00:03:12.680
I see. I will try different kinds.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:16.680
Please bring me only salads. 
I require no other foods.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.690
Should we make the individual 
salad's sizes smaller then?

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.210
That would be very nice.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.720
Understood.

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.230
<i>They surprised me at first, but then 
they showed their true colors.</i>

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:36.610
<i>Smaller sizes, meaning that they want to 
obfuscate their puny vegetable selection!</i>

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.090
<b>Caesar Salad With Warm Egg</b>

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.090
<b>Please enjoy the crispy salad 
together with the warm, soft egg</b>

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.090
Here you go.

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:43.050
The first salad is a Caesar 
salad with warm egg.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.020
Caesar, you say?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.840
It's best enjoyed after you mix 
in the egg that's perched on top.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:56.710
Here I go.

00:03:58.950 --> 00:03:59.980
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.920
<i>How refreshing!</i>

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.830
<i>But this egg's yolk is simply amazing.</i>

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.890
<i>It's transforming the 
dressing into rich sauce!</i>

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:14.790
<i>This tastiness is on par with the dishes 
from the banquet at the palace.</i>

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.290
Shinobu-san, did you always 
have this salad on the menu?

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.300
Ever since the Schnitzel incident, he's 
been wanting to expand our repertoire,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.170
and lately he's been into salads.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.170
I see.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:33.350
It seems that for our salad-loving guest 
here, that was perfectly timed.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.410
Was the salad good?

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.220
It was a truly marvelous salad.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.660
I finished it all.

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:43.410
Thank you very much.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.710
The next one is ready.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.280
Coming.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.960
<i>It was really a good salad.</i>

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:52.430
<i>The vegetables were very fresh, too.</i>

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.430
<i>However, each individual ingredient 
was very much normal!</i>

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.430
<i>This salad is not something 
that can shake Oilia!</i>

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.210
<b>Daikon Salad</b>

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.210
<b>The substantial texture of daikon and its 
refreshing quality make this a pleasure</b>

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.220
Next, we have a daikon salad.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.950
<i>Daikon? What is that?!</i>

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.910
<i>And what's with this 
dressing's creepy color?</i>

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.860
It can't be helped. This is all work.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.120
Huh?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:17.900
<i>The vegetable's water content and the 
sauce's saltiness pair quite well.</i>

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.900
At first, the color threw me off, 
but now I wonder what it is.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.140
This is a soy milk tarako sauce.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.580
Soy milk? Tarako?

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:31.890
Yes, soy milk is the juice 
squeezed from soy beans,

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.050
and tarako are eggs of an 
ocean fish called tara.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.280
Ocean?!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:42.380
When you mix this soy milk sauce with 
those eggs, it turns into that color.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.750
Taishou, another order of isobeage.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:47.550
Got it.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.590
<b>Crunch crunch crunch</b>

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:52.960
<i>Gah! Fish eggs, you say?!</i>

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:57.000
<b>Ocean</b>

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:57.000
<b>Here</b>

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.640
<i>Where do you think "here" is?</i>

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.070
<i>It's the landlocked Aitheria!</i>

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.460
<i>Oh, the canals!</i>

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:02.300
<i>Are you saying the canals' transportation 
system is so prosperous</i>

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:05.080
<i>that it can easily put fruits of the 
sea into the hands of commoners?!</i>

00:06:06.850 --> 00:06:11.090
<i>In order to prevent word of this prosperity 
getting out, they are hiding this information!</i>

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:18.960
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.210
<i>I was right to choose this place.</i>

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:18.950
<i>After all, I was able to glean all this 
information after just two plates!</i>

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.940
Oh my, this salad was amazing as well.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.440
Thank you so much.

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:24.700
The next one is ready.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:27.040
Next, we have a potato salad.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.620
Kartoffel...

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.530
I guess this is where the line ends.

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.300
It's good!

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.820
<i>I expected it to be Kartoffel 
and other scrap vegetables,</i>

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.810
<b>Potato Salad</b>

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.810
<b>Warm and scrumptious potato salad. 
Ground black sesame is Nobu's touch</b>

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.750
<i>but it's not that simplistic.</i>

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.650
<i>The Kartoffel has been processed 
to have a perfect texture,</i>

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.890
<i>and wonderfully contrasting it
 are the vegetables and sausage!</i>

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.240
<i>Then, enveloping everything, this sauce!</i>

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.530
Is it to your liking?

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.020
Yes!

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.970
It's a really delicious salad.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.220
Don't you think so?!

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:15.710
Mayonnaise and potato are a 
perfect pair, aren't they?!

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:21.620
<i>Mayonnaise? That seasoning alone can 
elevate Kartoffel to this level?</i>

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:23.350
Tada!

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.580
If you like that, would 
you like to try this?

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.610
S-Sure.

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.690
Please give that a try.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.000
<i>This scent...</i>

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.120
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.110
<i>pepper!</i>

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.130
Is that thing...

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:47.710
Yes, it's pepper.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.580
Just adding a tiny bit of pepper really 
kicks up the flavor, doesn't it?

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.610
When you put it on potato salad, it—

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.610
<i>What are you talking about?!</i>

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:58.000
<i>Of course it's tasty!</i>

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.620
<i>Pepper is traded at the same rate as gold!</i>

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.270
<i>As gold!</i>

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:07.980
<i>As if that's not enough, they 
are using it on a mere salad?!</i>

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:11.930
<i>I have to admit though, the 
potato salad with pepper is...</i>

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.040
<i>so good.</i>

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.980
<i>So does that mean Aitheria 
has the financial power</i>

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:19.030
<i>to use pepper as a daily condiment?</i>

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:23.270
<i>Our country has vastly underestimated 
the power of their empire.</i>

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.380
<i>I have to return at once 
and report my findings!</i>

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.380
Taishou, you're really going to serve that?

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:33.990
Of course. This is the one salad I've 
been wanting to serve all along!

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.100
<i>A-Are you telling me there's 
something even better?!</i>

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.760
<i>There's no way that something 
can surpass pepper!</i>

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:43.760
Here you go, Nobu's special, 
fruit salad No. 100.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:45.540
It's so shiny it's blinding me!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.640
What is this?!

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.130
<b>Fruit Salad No. 100</b>

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.130
<b>Please enjoy the subtlety that's quite 
contrary to its flashy appearance</b>

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.130
Wh-What is that on top?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.460
It's gold leaf.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.650
Gold leaf?!

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:56.520
Yes, it's made by stretching 
gold really thin.

00:08:56.520 --> 00:08:58.760
Is it edible?

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:02.010
It poses no risk to your health.

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:04.170
It's not nutritious either, though.

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:07.210
But isn't the color so nice?

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.660
<i>Are you telling me that's the 
sole reason they used gold?!</i>

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:13.790
<i>Is this the true power of the empire?!</i>

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:19.140
This is an odd bowl. Can 
this be eaten as well?

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.770
Yes, it's called dragon fruit.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:24.190
I had to go through some trouble 
to get it for this sala—

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.350
What's wrong?

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:31.110
D-D-D-Dragon?!

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:40.040
<i>This means that this gold, pepper, 
those fancy ingredients...</i>

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:42.800
<i>they are all linked to the 
treasure of a dragon.</i>

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:47.790
<i>What I should be in awe of is that these 
people stole a dragon's treasure.</i>

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.390
Thank you for the meal!

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:52.160
Sir?

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:55.830
See, you startled him and made him leave!

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.580
And what's with that No. 100 name?

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:00.970
Wasn't that the name of that 
golden robot you were building?

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:06.020
<i>Our country should not meddle with 
this country, with this restaurant!</i>

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:09.690
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:10.840
<i>This is what happened at this Izakaya Nobu.</i>

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:16.830
I will never set foot in that place again.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:20.190
However, Nobu's salads were all good.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.670
I wish I could eat them one more time.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:40.750
<b>Ningyouchou</b>

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:37.030
Nihonbashi's Ningyouchou.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.750
It's right in the middle 
of the Shitamachi area.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.430
By now, it's become a business district.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:44.830
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:44.320
It has.

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:48.160
That means it's has become a hotly contested 
area for drink and food places.

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:51.120
Hmm... but potato salad, huh?

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.210
You don't sound happy.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.130
<b>Tonjiru Restaurant</b>

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.220
This is tough one.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.140
Don't be like that.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:58.630
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.510
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.210
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu."

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:01.120
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:06.250
Potato salad should be available 
at any bar, anyone would say.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:07.820
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi</b>

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.840
This one's different!

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:07.840
Oh, here it is.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:16.750
<b>Ningyouchou
 Potato Salad</b>

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.980
I was told to go to Peshi.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.280
Let's go, then!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:13.720
That's right, here! Here!

00:11:14.090 --> 00:11:16.750
<b>Wajouryoushu Peshi</b>

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.750
Peshi is a sake bar with an 
impressive list of sake.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:19.550
We often order potato salad.

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:22.820
<b>Peshi
 Chef  Kabeyama Takahiro-san</b>

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:22.540
It may be rude to say this, but 
it's just potato salad then.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:23.740
You're going to get hate.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:28.470
But I was told by someone that 
it's actually different here.

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.470
That's right.

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:30.410
We have three different variations here.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.030
Oh, three kinds, then?

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.500
Salmon roe.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.780
Melted cheese.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.130
Oh my, this one's curry flavored.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:41.050
First, a good gulp of whatsontap.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:42.590
Here they are!

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.650
That looks good.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:46.110
This needs a bit more preparation.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:47.320
Huh?

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:51.000
They're going to torch that melty cheese!

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.010
This is so the cheese is completely melted.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.700
The cheese is bubbling.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:55.720
Those grill marks are so tempting.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:58.250
These are still all potato salads, right?

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.030
Yes, that's right. This is the 
curry flavored potato salad.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.170
<b>Curry flavored potato salad</b>

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.680
Curry flavor, huh? Let's try that.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:07.070
Isn't the curry flavor a good match?

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:10.180
I see. That's something I can get behind.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:11.390
See!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.080
They don't really do this, huh?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.320
It's quite rare, yes.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:16.120
When you make potato salad at home,

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:18.900
adding some curry powder could 
change it up quite a bit.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.220
Everyone, try this at home!

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:23.060
Now, the potato salad with salmon roe.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:24.420
<b>Potato salad with salmon roe</b>

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.100
How do you like the rubies of the sea?

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.960
Nobody would even think to do 
this, so nobody does, right?

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.070
Correct.

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.600
In order to make these pair better,

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:33.150
we directly smoke the potatoes and 
bacon using cherry wood chips.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.500
That's why it smells like that!

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:38.850
So to make it smokey, you're 
actually putting in that work.

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:40.870
Yes, that's the secret!

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:44.180
<b>Gratin style potato salad</b>

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.180
So you put cheese on top and 
then you torch it a bit, right?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.890
So? How is it? Tell me!

00:12:48.890 --> 00:12:50.870
This is clever.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.510
How's the flavor?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:52.050
It's good.

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.830
The potato and cheese go together so well!

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.830
Can't underestimate it 
because it's potato salad.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:57.680
See!

00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:01.240
I'm curious. What does the name 
of this place, "Peshi," stand for?

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.240
I was curious too!

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:05.270
It's a regional word from Iwate. It's like 
a filler word at the end of a sentence.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.220
Something something peshi.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:09.430
This is potato salad peshi. Like that?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:09.950
Well...

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.300
Stop bullying him peshi!

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:13.540
I'm not quite sure.

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.450
All three variations were quite excellent.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.710
And the beer?

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.580
A great match!

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.080
I bet!

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.610
Even Nagira-san approves 
of "Wajouryoushu Peshi".

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:28.020
It's a one minute walk 
from Ningyouchou station.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.060
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:31.690
If you want to have good potato 
salad, come here. Come here!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:58.010
<b>Next Time...
Kabayaki Without Honor</b>

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:54.420
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:57.470
Please sample the tasty tales.
